   837799   1.687179         0.102217           0.102217
  8400511   1.675781         0.090819           0.090819

  V. WHAT DOMINATES D(n)?  (the terminal small-odd visits)
  --------------------------------------------------

  ln(1+1/(3a)) ~ 1/(3a): a single visit to a is worth ~1/(3a) in D.
  Large values along the orbit contribute negligibly; the defect is
  accumulated almost entirely in the last few odd values before 1.
  Single-visit weights:
     a=   1: ln(1+1/(3a)) = 0.287682   <- terminal a=1 dominates
     a=   3: ln(1+1/(3a)) = 0.105361
     a=   5: ln(1+1/(3a)) = 0.064539
     a=   7: ln(1+1/(3a)) = 0.046520
     a=  11: ln(1+1/(3a)) = 0.029853
     a=  21: ln(1+1/(3a)) = 0.015748
     a=  85: ln(1+1/(3a)) = 0.003914
     a= 341: ln(1+1/(3a)) = 0.000977

  D(27) = 0.181362; top contributors (value a : share of D):
